Z||000000||Raydar||12-10-1999||07:31 PM||||Is the 88 front wheel bearing / hub assembly pressed into the steering knuckle? I've got the three bolts out, but the sucker won't budge. If it's not pressed in, it's rusted in. (I have the utmost faith in "Liquid Wrench".) Any ideas? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pretender||12-11-1999||02:23 AM||||Mine was really tight, i ended up tapping it out from the back, but watch out because when mine finally broke it's seal and poped out it came down next to my knee. just keep at it, it'll loosen.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Raydar||12-11-1999||10:00 AM||||Pretender... Thanks! I'll give that a try, now that it's had time to marinate in the Liquid Wrench. So far, a crowbar and a B.F. screwdriver have been completely useless. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-11-1999||06:38 PM||||Well... Where skill and finesse failed, ignorance and brute force prevailed. A crowbar (bent), a B.F. screwdriver (with a broken tip), and a B.F. hammer... The sucker finally came out. Badly dented, but out, nevertheless. But it *really* didn't want to.<BR>Thought I was gonna have to find a machine shop with a press (or something). Thanks. Pretender!<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-11-1999).]||||reg||1
